<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/19th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Wad Ras</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1860">1860</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hispano-moroccan-war-1859-1860">Hispano-Moroccan War (1859–1860)</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Wad <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ras">Ras</a> was signed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tetouan">Tetouan</a> on 26 April 1860, ending the Hispano-Moroccan War. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/morocco">Morocco</a> agreed to enlarge the territory of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ceuta">Ceuta</a>, pay <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> a large indemnity and cede a territory on the Atlantic coast at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/santa-cruz-de-mar-pequena">Santa Cruz de Mar Pequeña</a>, later identified with Ifni. Tetouan was held by Spain until the indemnity was paid in 1862.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/treaty-of-wad-ras.jpg" alt="Treaty of Wad Ras" width="320" height="181" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Joaquín Domínguez Bécquer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:La_Paz_de_Wad-Ras.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
